	abstract = {Leprosy is a neglected skin infectious disease caused mainly by Mycobacterium leprae. It is annually reported in the South-East Asia Region in the majority and underserved areas. Early diagnosis is essential to eliminate leprosy since the real causes of contamination besides the untreated patients are unclear and it can cause a lot of damage if it is not treated. Considering a diagnostic done from images could be appropriate because the current diagnosis is clinical and sometimes in case of complication. AI/ML has proven to be reliable in predictions or diagnostics of human infections from numerical data making use of algorithms that can analyze, identify patterns, and make predictions with minimal human intervention. Among those algorithms, the Convolutional Neural Network and the Support vector machine have been chosen for the leprosy image analysis in this paper due to their performance in analyzing images.},
